/** CPE-49 strong-retrofit batch 7 (final batch -- upgrade to the 4-case standard: Sample +
 * boundary + tricky + stress, completing all 49). Boundary cases are the exact ones from the
 * original seed-cpe49-batch7.ts, re-verified against freshly written reference solutions.
 * Wherever this project's own scraped Sample had a richer multi-case dataset beyond the boundary
 * (6 of the 7 problems here did), it was checked first -- catching two real bugs in
 * uva-10222-decode-the-mad-man before trusting the solution for new cases:
 * (1) the decoded output does NOT preserve the input's original case (an uppercase 'K' decodes to
 *     lowercase 'h', not 'H' -- the boundary alone couldn't reveal this since it never mixed case
 *     expectations, but the real 19-line sample did);
 * (2) the scraped input's CRLF line endings were leaking a literal '\r' into decoded output when
 *     read line-by-line, invisible in a plain diff but caught by comparing raw bytes.
 * Both fixed and reconfirmed against the full sample before generating tricky/stress.
 *
 * Every other problem in this batch matched its full rich official sample on the first attempt:
 * - uva-10409-die-game: face-rotation state machine (top/bottom/north/south/east/west), matched
 *   dozens of real command sequences.
 * - uva-10415-eb-alto-saxophone-player: matched the real sample; tricky here specifically checks
 *   a strictly-shrinking finger-subset run (c,d,e,f,g each needs a subset of the previous note's
 *   fingers), which presses nothing after the first note -- a case the sample itself didn't
 *   directly exercise.
 * - uva-11321-sort-sort-and-sort: matched the real ~14000-byte sample, confirming both the
 *   C-style negative modulo (-100 mod 3 = -1, per the spec's own example) and the
 *   odd-before-even/descending-odd/ascending-even tiebreak rules.
 * - uva-118-mutant-flatworld-explorers: matched the real sample; tricky uses this problem's own
 *   widely-known canonical 3-robot 5x3-grid example as an independent cross-check beyond this
 *   project's scraped data.
 * - uva-11150-cola: only a 1-line official sample existed (same as the boundary), so N=1..200
 *   (the full stated input range) is used entirely as the stress case instead, giving complete
 *   coverage of the borrow-up-to-2-bottles technique across every legal input.
 * - uva-10189-minesweeper: the original batch7 already confirmed this sample was clean.
 */
